# PlayMaidan

A full-stack sports facility booking platform where customers discover and book turfs/courts in real time, and owners manage facilities, slots, and revenue — built with React, Node.js/Express, PostgreSQL (Prisma), and Socket.io.

## Demo

- **Live Demo:** https://turfly.vercel.app/

## 📸 Screenshots

### Owner
![PlayMaidan owner ](./screenshots/image-1.png)

### Customer 
![PlayMaidan customer](./screenshots/image-2.png)

## Features

### Customer
- Discover nearby facilities via location-based search
- View courts and a real-time slot availability grid
- Book a slot and pay online through Razorpay
- View booking history and cancel bookings
- Join a waitlist for full slots (notified by email if one opens up)

### Owner
- Create and manage multiple facilities with image uploads
- Add courts and bulk-generate time slots for a date range
- View bookings and an analytics dashboard (revenue, occupancy trends)
- Delete courts/facilities with password re-verification for facility deletion

### Platform
- Role-based access (`OWNER` / `CUSTOMER`)
- Real-time slot updates across all connected clients
- Concurrency-safe booking — no double-booking under simultaneous requests

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React (Vite), React Router, TanStack Query, Tailwind CSS, Leaflet, Recharts, Socket.io-client |
| Backend | Node.js, Express, Socket.io |
| Database | PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM |
| Authentication | JWT (access + refresh tokens) |
| Payments | Razorpay |
| Storage | Cloudinary (image uploads) |
| Email | EmailJS |
| Maps/Location | Leaflet + OpenStreetMap Nominatim (geocoding), Haversine-based distance search |
| Deployment | Vercel (frontend) | Render (Backend)

## 🔑 Key Technical Highlights

- **Concurrency-safe slot locking** — uses atomic `updateMany` operations that only lock a slot if it is still `AVAILABLE`, ensuring only one concurrent request can acquire the slot and preventing double-booking.

- **JWT authentication & refresh-token rotation** — uses short-lived access tokens with hashed refresh tokens that are rotated on every refresh.

- **Role-based authorization** — middleware enforces `OWNER`/`CUSTOMER` permissions, while controllers additionally verify resource ownership.

- **Verified payments** — Razorpay payment signatures are recomputed and verified server-side using HMAC-SHA256 before confirming a booking.

- **Real-time booking updates** — Socket.io broadcasts slot-status changes to connected clients, allowing availability to update without a page refresh.

- **Time-zone-aware booking logic** — compares slot times using `Asia/Kolkata` to correctly disable expired slots regardless of the server's timezone.
## System Architecture

```
React Client (Vite)
      │
      ├── REST API ────────► Node.js + Express
      │                            │
      └── WebSocket (Socket.io) ◄──┤
                                   Prisma ORM
                                    │
                              PostgreSQL

External services: Razorpay (payments), Cloudinary (image storage), EmailJS (transactional email)
```

## Booking Flow

```
Select Slot
   │
   ▼
Lock Slot (atomic update: AVAILABLE → LOCKED)
   │
   ▼
Create Razorpay Order
   │
   ▼
Razorpay Checkout
   │
   ▼
Verify Payment Signature (HMAC-SHA256)
   │
   ▼
Confirm Booking (slot → BOOKED, payment → PAID)
   │
   ▼
Real-time Slot Update (Socket.io)
   │
   ▼
Email Notification (customer + owner)
```

If the customer abandons checkout, the pending booking is deleted and the slot returns to `AVAILABLE`.

## Database Design

```
User
├── Facility (owner)
│     └── Court
│           └── Slot
│                 ├── Booking
│                 │     └── Payment
│                 └── Waitlist
└── Booking / Waitlist (customer)
```

