## Getting Started

```bash
# 1. Clone
git clone <repo-url>
cd turf-main

# 2. Install dependencies
cd server && npm install
cd ../client && npm install

# 3. Configure environment variables (see below)

# 4. Set up the database
cd server
npx prisma migrate dev
npx prisma generate
node prisma/seed.js        # optional: demo data

# 5. Start backend
npm run dev                 # http://localhost:5000

# 6. Start frontend (new terminal)
cd ../client
npm run dev                 # http://localhost:5173
```

## Environment Variables

**`server/.env`**
```
DATABASE_URL
ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY
REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID
EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY
EMAILJS_PRIVATE_KEY
EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID
PORT
NODE_ENV
FRONTEND_URL
```

**`client/.env`**
```
VITE_API_URL
```

## Testing

A concurrency test (`server/tests/concurrent-booking.test.js`) fires five simultaneous booking requests at the same slot to verify that only one succeeds and the rest are rejected — validating the atomic slot-locking logic under real race conditions.

## Deployment

- **Frontend:** Vercel (see `client/vercel.json`)
- **Backend:** Render

